===A5_S4_D4===
// attached to a log
Narrator: Being on Thavmia has really made you feel small.
Narrator: Not in a powerless or insignificant way — but in the sense of realising where you might stand in terms of the island and its inhabitants. As a part of a wider world, which you’ve only just discovered five days ago.
Narrator: …It’s not so bad, to be honest. There’s a bunch of people of the same size as you.
Narrator: And smaller, too, like the cotton critter you saved…
Noelle: (The Great Disaster really must be a huge size, to cause floods all over the Earth.) #portrait:NoelleUm
Narrator: Amelia notices you a little lost in thought.
Amelia: Hey! Noelle, what's with that look? Do you need more supplies from Rowan after all? #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Noelle: No, it’s not that. #portrait:NoelleUm
Amelia: So why are you so unhappy? #portrait:AmeliaSilly
Noelle: I’m just thinking about Noah’s story. #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Narrator: Amelia squints at you, realising it’s not <i>sadness,</i> but rather— 
Amelia: Oh, don’t tell me you want to do something crazy! #portrait:AmeliaShut
Noelle: I’m not going to go and find the Great Disaster or anything! #portrait:NoelleSad
Noelle: …It’d be impossible to build a boat for that, in a month’s time. #portrait:NoelleWhat
Noelle: (But… there’s a feeling in my gut that suggests there’s more to all of this.) #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
+[The Great Disaster…]
    -> choicehope
+[The weather…]
    -> choicehope
===choicehope===
Noelle: Don’t you think that with the Great Disaster’s size, it could affect more than just the floods? #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Noelle: Even a small breeze can cause stirring in the sea. If it wanted to, surely it could start a storm somewhere that’s normally free from bad weather. #portrait:NoelleUm
Noelle: (I’m not saying that the Great Disaster is a villain, but wouldn’t it make sense if it was aiming for Thavmia somehow, as it’s where Noah set up his base?) #portrait:NoelleUm
Noelle: (If I was wronged, or perhaps disrespected and angry, I might resort to such actions, too. Knocking on their door.) #portrait:NoelleUm
Amelia: Noelle… Even if that were true, and it’s the one causing the storms — you don’t have proof. #portrait:AmeliaShut
Amelia: And unless the Elders have a magical way to speak to the Kraken that we don’t know about, there’s no way to confirm or appease it either. #portrait:AmeliaShut
Noelle: …I know. But I can’t put off the feeling that there’s another clue somewhere that just hasn’t been found. Like the box I managed to open for Cillian. #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Narrator: Amelia studies your expression once more.
Amelia: This is important to you, isn’t it? #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Amelia: Is it because you think Noah might be your ancestor? #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Narrator: A beat passes. You give Amelia a small smile.
Noelle: I guess… I’d feel like I’ve fulfilled my purpose, if that is the case. #portrait:NoelleSad
Noelle: That I washed up here for a reason. #portrait:NoelleSad
Noelle: (That I was chased out of home, and fled, for a reason.) #portrait:NoelleUm
Amelia: …Alright, I get it. #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Amelia: Let’s go back to Rowan’s house and demand for fabric again. And ask Cillian if he’s got any more info before heading to the northern beach. #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Amelia: I’ve heard that the Ichthyos are familiar with seaside caves. Noah probably used them at some point. #portrait:AmeliaHappy
Noelle: Amelia… Thank you! #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Amelia: Hmph. #portrait:AmeliaHostile
Amelia: But if this search comes up empty, you better be ready to rake up merit points with the settlements! #portrait:AmeliaHostile
Amelia: We are not waiting out the floods outside of the mountains! #portrait:AmeliaHostile
Noelle: Yes, ma’am! #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
-> DONE